column30:
User accounts (not admin accounts) can be granted the role "translation_admin", which allows them to:

* Add or modify [locales|https://test.archiveofourown.org/locales].
* Add or modify [languages|https://test.archiveofourown.org/languages] (although unlike locales, the UI doesn't show them the buttons/forms to do so).

Redundantly, all of these actions can also be done by any admin account, regardless of admin roles. Let's clean this up:

* Remove all mentions of the "translation_admin" role in the code base (permission checks, utility methods on the User model, factories, specs fixtures, database seeding fixtures).
* Add a rake task to remove "translation_admin" from the roles table.

Finally, restrict access to locales and languages to admins with roles: superadmin, translation. Only admin with said roles will:

* have the "Locales" menu in the admin navigation;
* see the "Add a Language" and "Edit" buttons on [languages|https://test.archiveofourown.org/languages];
* see the [locales|https://test.archiveofourown.org/locales] table with "Edit" buttons and the "New Locale" option;
* not be redirected and given an error message if they enter the URL to post [https://test.archiveofourown.org/locales/new|https://test.archiveofourown.org/locales/new)] or edit [https://test.archiveofourown.org/locales/en/edit|https://test.archiveofourown.org/locales/en/edit)] a locale.

*Deploy notes*

{{bundle exec rake After:remove_translation_admin_role}}

