h1. Steps to reproduce

# Log in as a wrangler (e.g., testy) or an admin
# Go to [https://test.archiveofourown.org/tag_wranglers/t3sty|https://test.archiveofourown.org/tag_wranglers/t3sty] (you can use the name of any nonexistent user here)

h1. What happens

A 500 error.

h1. What should happen

A 404.

h1. Notes

You have to be logged in as a wrangler or an admin; if you're not, you'll just get an access denied message (the specific one depends on whether you're logged in or out). 

The error happens because [we basically don't account for the possibility the user might not exist|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/3d246f54ce2009468c47c34eba54d43bd27a8711/app/controllers/tag_wranglers_controller.rb#L38-L51]:

{code:ruby}  def show
    @wrangler = User.find_by(login: params[:id])
    @page_subtitle = @wrangler.login
    @fandoms = @wrangler.fandoms.by_name
    @counts = {}
    [Fandom, Character, Relationship, Freeform].each do |klass|
      @counts[klass.to_s.downcase.pluralize.to_sym] = Rails.cache.fetch("/wrangler/counts/sidebar/#{klass}", race_condition_ttl: 10, expires_in: 1.hour) do
        klass.unwrangled.in_use.count
      end
    end
    @counts[:UnsortedTag] = Rails.cache.fetch("/wrangler/counts/sidebar/UnsortedTag", race_condition_ttl: 10, expires_in: 1.hour) do
      UnsortedTag.count
    end
  end{code}

