column151:
01/Sep/22 7:36 AM;557058:fa089759-8cd1-4db3-b506-5731a37fd5a6;After 11 failed login attempts, I got a “Retry later” page with the header:

{noformat}retry-after: 132{noformat}

I assumed that the other limits were much higher and harder to hit by hand, so I used a curl command to fetch a bunch of similar URLs in sequence and record the headers (with the {{user_credentials}} cookie set to make sure that nothing was cached):

{noformat}curl -k --dump-header FILENAME -o /dev/null \
  -b "user_credentials=1" \
  "https://test.archiveofourown.org/?try=[1-200]" \
  --user USER:PASSWORD{noformat}

I assumed that a lot of the timeout periods were based around 5 minute or 10 minute intervals, so I spaced out my tests by 10 minutes and tried to start them when the last clock digit was 0 or 1.

* For the homepage, I got a “Retry later” after 121 tries with the header:
** {noformat}retry-after: 357{noformat}
* For {{/tags/Testing/works}}, I got a “Retry later” after 71 tries with the header:
** {noformat}retry-after: 506{noformat}
* For {{/tags/Testing/bookmarks}}, I got a “Retry later” after 31 tries with the header:
** {noformat}retry-after: 497{noformat}

Looks good to me\!

