column30:
When checking for spam (e.g., on logged-out comments and abuse reports), we’re seeing a small number of 500 errors (trace below).

This appears to be because Akismetor uses URI.escape, [which was removed in Ruby 3.0|https://github.com/ruby/uri/issues/14].

*Testing*

Log out and make sure you can leave a comment. 

Make sure such comments can still get marked as spam. To force a comment to be marked as spam by Akismet, fill in the “Guest name” field with “viagra-test-123” (minus the quotation marks).

*Error*

Error class: NoMethodError

Transaction name: [comments#create|https://one.newrelic.com/nr1-core/errors/overview/MTE1ODkyfEFQTXxBUFBMSUNBVElPTnwxOTAwMzQ?account=115892&duration=1800000&state=9e6c6f5d-14bc-6019-3dea-9a6943cb0a0d]

undefined method `escape' for URI:Module

//home/ao3app/app/shared/bundle/ruby/3:00/gems/akismetor-1
//home/ao3app/app/shared/bundle/ruby/3:00/gems/akismetor-1
//home/ao3app/app/shared/bundle/ruby/3:00/gems/akismetor-1
//home/ao3app/app/releases/20230108154518/app/models/comment:rb:444:in 'check_for_spam?'
//home/ao3app/app/releases/20230108154518/app/models/comment:rb:55:in 'check_for_spam'

MariaDB support says:

{quote}One more thing which may be causing the query performance differences MariaDB vs Percona are tables without without primary keys.  We strongly recommend against tables without primary keys, they are terrible for performance in MariaDB{quote}

roles_users and schema_migrations need primary keys to improve performance. 

The tables in question are {{roles_users}}, and {{schema_migrations}}

*Testing*

In addition to running the migrations, log in as an admin who can modify roles and ensure you can add/remove roles from a user.

*Deploy notes:*

The migrations should be run before deploying:

{{bundle exec rake db:migrate:up VERSION=20230113225105}}

{{bundle exec rake db:migrate:up VERSION=20230113225128}}

