column154:
21/Feb/23 4:22 PM;629dc33e9b728c006a926594;To expand on Sarken’s comment about testing, after the new PR to allow this gets merged,

{code:html}<details open> <summary>Automated Status: Operational</summary> <p>Velocity: 12m/s</p> <p>Direction: North</p> </details>{code}

should be allowed anywhere a {{<details>}} is allowed, and adding it should cause the details element to be open by default, instead of starting off closed. You can set a value for open, but it will be ignored--for display purposes, what matters is whether or not the {{open}} is  there, not what its value is, so {{open="false"}} will start off open by default, just like {{open}} or {{open="true"}}.

