column30:
It all begins with a Rails security update ([https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-6367|https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-6367|smart-link]) that prevents the YAML loader to use classes outside of an [allowlist|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/b36c43d281b8db77f410e0d014bdb1319a3fb3f4/config/application.rb#L78-L79].

On staging and production, we have users whose passwords were created back when we used Authlogic instead of Devise for authentication. Such passwords use the class [BCrypt::Password|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/b36c43d281b8db77f410e0d014bdb1319a3fb3f4/lib/backwards_compatible_password_decryptor.rb#L24] from the bcrypt gem. If they end up in user audits (the {{audited_changes}} field), they can be not be loaded normally:

{noformat}/home/ao3app/.rvm/rubies/ruby-3.0.5/lib/ruby/3.0.0/psych/class_loader.rb:99:in `find': Tried to load unspecified class: BCrypt::Password (Psych::DisallowedClass){noformat}

When we log password changes in user audits, we really only care that it changes, we don’t need to log the actual encrypted password values. To fix this:

* add BCrypt::Password to {{config.active_record.yaml_column_permitted_classes}} so old audit entries can be loaded;
* use [the redacted option|https://github.com/collectiveidea/audited/pull/485] of the audited gem on the password fields ({{encrypted_password}}, {{password_salt}});
* -and because audited has some- [-bugs with the redacted option-|https://github.com/collectiveidea/audited/pull/628]-, update the gem to 5.3.0.- Audited updated to 5.3 in [AO3-6562|https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/browse/AO3-6562]

h1. Testing

On staging, older users e.g. testy has BCrypt::Password in audits. Make sure this script doesn’t stall with Psych::DisallowedClass:

{code:ruby}user = User.find_by(login: "testy")
user.audits.each { |a| puts a.inspect }; nil{code}

Then ask some users to change password and check that the password change is saved as {{"encrypted_password"=>"[REDACTED]"}}).

