14/Aug/23 5:28 PM;557058:443ab871-4096-403e-bd6f-f3534fe417f0;I think I’ve found a bug with the CSS.

I logged in as orphan_account on staging, which has no favorite tags, no inbox, and no marked for later items. I ended up with a big gap on the upper right, probably because it relies on this to make the grid:

{noformat}.logged-in .splash > div:nth-of-type(odd) { 
  clear: left;
}{noformat}

And when you have no favorite tags, the first div (which is an odd number) is actually the second module, so it gets pushed down to the second row.

I was able to reproduce by removing all of testy8’s favorite tags.

!Screenshot 2023-08-14 at 8.27.12 PM.png|width=83.33333333333334%,alt="Homepage, with a big empty space next to Find Your Favorites."!

