column30:
Admins with the superadmin, docs, support, and translation roles should be able to post, modify, and delete FAQs. (Bonus points if admins with the translation role can only modify FAQs that are translations! But we can push this to a separate issue for later.)

Admins without those roles should:

* not have the “Archive FAQ” option under “Admin Posts” in the admin navigation menu
* not have the “Archive FAQ” in the admin navigation buttons ({{app/views/admin/_admin_nav.html.erb}}), shown on pages like the wrangling guidelines page when logged in as a tag wrangling admin 
* get the regular, non-admin version of the [FAQ index|https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq] when following the “FAQ” link in the main navigation or otherwise attempting to access the URL for the FAQ index ({{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq}})
* not have the “Updated: [Date]” info or “Edit” link in an h2 on the top of the page when accessing a specific category (e.g., {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name?language_id=en}})
** i.e., it should look the same as it does when _not_ logged in as admin
* be redirected and given an error message if they enter the following URLs 
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/new?language_id=en}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/manage?language_id=en}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name/edit?language_id=en}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name/questions/manage}}
** {{https://test.archiveofourown.org/faq/category_name/confirm_delete?language_id=en}}

*Testing note*: In the above URLs, {{category_name}} is a placeholder needs to be replaced with an FAQ category that is available on staging such as {{posting-and-editing}} or {{collections-and-challenges}}.

