column30:
h1. Steps to reproduce

# Log in
# Choose an adventure:
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > My Work Skins > Create Work Skin
# Enter CSS like {{.a { color-scheme: dark }}}
# Submit

h1. What happens

An error saying {{color-scheme}} is not allowed.

h1. What should happen

It should be possible to make a site or work skin using the [color-scheme CSS property|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color-scheme] to control whether certain elements (e.g., scroll bars and form elements) should be shown in the system’s dark or light mode. 

All of the following values should be allowed:

{noformat}color-scheme: normal;
color-scheme: light;
color-scheme: dark;
color-scheme: light dark;
color-scheme: dark light;
color-scheme: only light;
color-scheme: only dark;
color-scheme: inherit;
color-scheme: initial;
color-scheme: revert;
color-scheme: revert-layer;
color-scheme: unset;{noformat}

h1. Testing

Put the following into a skin and make sure that after saving, the output matches the input and you don't get any error messages. Note that this won’t actually lead to any visual changes; we’re just trying to make sure all the values are accepted by our system. 

{noformat}.a { color-scheme: normal; }
.b { color-scheme: light; }
.c { color-scheme: dark; }
.d { color-scheme: light dark; }
.e { color-scheme: dark light; }
.f { color-scheme: only light; }
.g { color-scheme: only dark; }
.h { color-scheme: inherit; }
.i { color-scheme: initial; }
.j { color-scheme: revert; }
.k { color-scheme: revert-layer; }
.l { color-scheme: unset; }{noformat}

You’ll also need to check the skins help file – the ? by the CSS field – and make sure the new properties are all listed.

*Deploy Notes*

This requires running the recache skins playbook (it does all static assets not just skins).

