column30:
We’d like to allow use of [aspect-ratio|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/aspect-ratio] in skins. 

For values, it should accept:

#  the {{auto}} keyword
# whole numbers ({{1}})
# decimal numbers ({{0.5}})
# [ratios|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/ratio] ({{16/9}}), which should be allowed to have 
## spaces before the slash
## spaces after the slash
## spaces both before and after the slash
## spaces on neither side of the slash
## decimals
# the {{auto}} keyword *before* a 
## whole number,
## decimal number, or
## ratio
# the auto keyword *after* a
## whole number, 
## decimal number, or
## ratio

The help popup at [https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html|https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html] will also need to be updated:

# {{aspect-ratio}} will need to be listed under “We also allow the following specific properties”
# the “Numeric Values” section will need to be updated according to the fix:
## assuming the fix only allows ratios for {{aspect-ratio}}, this sentence should be added above the “PS”: “For the aspect-ratio property, you can specify ratios using numeric values up to three decimal places."
## if ratios have to be allowed everywhere numbers are accepted, the text should instead be amended to say: “You can specify numeric values up to three decimal places, either as percentages or ratios or in [various units|https://w3schools.com/css/css_units.asp]:” (the “or ratios” is new)

h1. Testing

To test, you can just make sure our CSS sanitizer accepts the property and the desired formats for the values. Whether or not they work is the browser’s problem, not ours. 😆 

# Log in
# Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
# Fill in the Title field
# Next to the “CSS” heading/label, use the “?” help symbol to open the help pop-up and ensure it includes the text provided above.
# Close the help pop-up
# Enter the CSS provided below these instructions in the CSS field
# Press Submit

All but the last four rules ({{.invalid1}}, {{.invalid2}}, {{.invalid3}}, and {{.invalid4}}) in this CSS should be permitted.

{code:css}.class1 { aspect-ratio: banana }
.class2 { aspect-ratio: 1 }
.class3 { aspect-ratio: 0.5 }
.class4a { aspect-ratio: 16 /9 }
.class4b { aspect-ratio: 16/ 9 }
.class4c { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9}
.class4d { aspect-ratio: 16/9 }
.class4e { aspect-ratio: 1/1.75 }
.class5a { aspect-ratio: auto 1 }
.class5b { aspect-ratio: auto 0.25 }
.class5c { aspect-ratio: auto 4/3 }
.class6a { aspect-ratio: 1 auto }
.class6b { aspect-ratio: 0.25 auto }
.class6c { aspect-ratio: 0.5/ 1 auto }
.invalid1 { aspect-ratio: 1,300 }
.invalid2 { aspect-ratio: 100% }
.invalid3 { aspect-ratio: auto
auto ; }
.invalid4 {
  aspect-ratio: 1
auto
url(http://foo.com/bar.png);
}{code}

The help text at [https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html|https://test.archiveofourown.org/help/skins-creating.html] says:

{quote}We allow external image URLs (specified as url('http://somesite.com/my_awesome_image.jpg') in JPG, GIF, and PNG formats.{quote}

Let’s change that to [https://example.com/my_awesome_image.jpg|https://example.com/my_awesome_image.jpg] instead, since [example.com|http://example.com] exists for this purpose and can never be bought for nefarious purposes.

column156:
14/Feb/25 9:41 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;{quote}finding the {{rubygems}} version was incompatible{quote}

For the record, from the error logged ({{undefined method `ignored?'}}), I found [the rubygems change that introduced the method|https://github.com/rubygems/rubygems/commit/c80998a22ad06e3bf31347cde446d3f64b1f5c65]. The tags on this commit show that the change is available in rubygems 3.6+ and bundler 2.6+.

We are up-to-date on bundler ([2.6.3|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/e44c57109b36316d6dd2704ce8afa54da1d74370/Gemfile.lock#L791]) but behind on rubygems on our app servers:

{code:none}$ gem --version
3.4.19{code}

so the fix is to run {{rvm rubygems 3.6.0}} on all app servers.

