h1. Steps to reproduce

# Log in
# Choose an adventure:
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > My Work Skins > Create Work Skin
# Enter CSS like {{.a { accent-color: #900 }}}
# Submit

h1. What happens

An error saying {{accent-color}} is not allowed.

h1. What should happen

It should be possible to make a site or work skin using the [accent-color CSS property|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/accent-color] to control the color used on certain form elements (e.g., checked checkboxes).

All of the following values should be allowed:

{noformat}accent-color: darkred;
accent-color: #900;
accent-color: rgb(0 200 0);
accent-color: hsl(228 4% 24%);{noformat}

h1. Testing

Put the following into a skin and make sure that after saving, the output matches the input and you don't get any error messages. Note that this won’t actually lead to any visual changes; we’re just trying to make sure all the values are accepted by our system. 

{noformat}.a { accent-color: darkred; }
.b { accent-color: #900; }
.c { accent-color: rgb(0 200 0); }
.d { accent-color: hsl(228 4% 24%); }{noformat}

You’ll also need to check the skins help file – the ? by the CSS field – and make sure the new property is listed.

*Deploy Notes*

This requires running the recache skins playbook (it does all static assets not just skins).

